From 1cca9db782f55c2bd592870ff4b7ce6ca71ab923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:09:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ksmbd: require user stream xattrs

get_file_stream_info() assumes every xattr name can contain the full
"user.DosStream." prefix.  It compares DosStream at a fixed offset
without first checking the "user." prefix.  A short name can make the
comparison read past its NUL.  A non-user xattr with matching bytes at
that offset can be misread using the stream-name offsets.

Check that the xattr name is long enough to contain the encoded stream
prefix, and require the exact "user.DosStream." prefix before
interpreting the remainder as a stream name.  This keeps the fixed
offsets within the xattr name and limits enumeration to the namespace
used for ksmbd streams.

Reachable over the network from an authenticated client:

  SMB2 QUERY_INFO
    -> smb2_query_info()
    -> SMB2_O_INFO_FILE -> smb2_get_info_file()
    -> FILE_STREAM_INFORMATION -> get_file_stream_info()
    -> ksmbd_vfs_listxattr(), then strncmp at fixed offset 5 per xattr

Triggering the original misread also needs the file to already carry a
matching xattr: a name shorter than the fixed offset (typically only on
filesystems that allow non-standard names, e.g. FUSE), or a non-user
xattr whose bytes at offset 5 equal "DosStream.".  The remote query path
itself is reachable; the faulty state requires prior local,
cross-protocol, or special-backend-filesystem setup.

Signed-off-by: Haofeng Li <lihaofeng@kylinos.cn>
Reviewed-by: ChenXiaoSong <chenxiaosong@kylinos.cn>
---
 fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
index f01c2c8d2ed8..0154348af799 100644
--- a/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/smb2pdu.c
@@ -6558,7 +6558,10 @@ static int get_file_stream_info(struct ksmbd_work *work,
 
 		ksmbd_debug(SMB, "%s, len %d\n", stream_name, streamlen);
 
-		if (strncmp(&stream_name[XATTR_USER_PREFIX_LEN],
+		if (streamlen < XATTR_NAME_STREAM_LEN ||
+		    strncmp(stream_name, XATTR_USER_PREFIX,
+			    XATTR_USER_PREFIX_LEN) ||
+		    strncmp(&stream_name[XATTR_USER_PREFIX_LEN],
 			    STREAM_PREFIX, STREAM_PREFIX_LEN))
 			continue;
 
